    "title": "Upcoming lane restrictions for Route 15 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylynne Enloe ,\n8 hours ago\nTIOGA COUNTY, Pa. ( WETM ) – According to a release from the Pennsylvania Department of Transportation (PennDOT), lanes will be restricted in both directions of I-99/Route 15 in Lawrence Township for a paving project.\nOn Friday, Oct. 23, and Monday, Oct. 26, the project contractor will pave before the bridges over the Cowanesque River near the intersection with Route 49. Weather permitting, drivers can anticipate alternating lane restrictions during daylight hours.\nROADWORK This $6,036,000 project consists of on/off ramp resurfacing and bridge preservation work, including milling, base repairs, paving, concrete deck repairs, epoxy overlay, guiderail upgrades, line painting and other construction work.\nAnyone interested in monitoring major road conditions can visit www.511PA.com .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WETM - MyTwinTiers.com.",
    "summary": "TIOGA COUNTY, Pa. ( WETM ) – According to a release from the Pennsylvania Department of Transportation (PennDOT), lanes will be restricted in both directions of I-99/Route 15 in Lawrence Township for a paving project. On Friday, Oct. 23, and Monday, Oct. 26, the project contractor will pave before the bridges over the Cowanesque River near the intersection with Route 49. Weather permitting, drivers can anticipate alternating lane restrictions during daylight hours.",
